  note     = {kind=finding by=substrate. W4 file 4 cut 5, tick 44. The origin's _log_index (once 71 percent of a 912s suite before memoisation) is nondeterministic on a module logged under two hash dirs because os.walk order is the filesystem's; log_index sorts. Consumers figures.py:846 and stale_error_logs.py:48 reach log_is_fresh through split_pipeline. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): W4 file 4 cut 5 (tick 44): substrate/log_freshness.py carries split_census.log_is_fresh + _log_index as log_is_fresh(src_rel, dag, index, mtime_of, root) / freshness / newest_dependency / log_index(build_dir) / mtime_on_disk - the DAG (disk, deps, src_to_mod), the log index and the mtime reader all parameters. The origin's three recorded silent failures (string-surgery module names not in the DAG, an added agda/ prefix, a bare except around getmtime that made every log read fresh) are cases that cannot be silent: withheld verdict, prefix stripped never added, unreadable dependency -> UNSAFE stale with the count. 14/14 over a fake DAG (transitive A->B->C stale with the culprit named) and a temp _build tree. FINDING from the differential: the origin's _log_index walks with os.walk, so which hash dir wins for a module logged under two is NONDETERMINISTIC (filesystem order); log_index sorts, so the pick is stable. The differential asserts the origin's pick is one of the candidates, never a specific one.}
}

