  check    = {selftest:uv,run,python,substrate/sync_verdict_selftest.py,--selftest},
  note     = {kind=finding by=build-oracle. Ruled 2026-09-20 (W8): use cputime for the timing gate, not wall. The apex gate had crossed a 120s wall ceiling three times for unchanged work (120.2s quiet, 120.3s alone, 46s a minute earlier); measured alone after the repair: 54.7s wall, 54.6s CPU, CPU-bound and under the ceiling. sync_verdict carries both clocks per row and an over_ceiling property on CPU; the wall guard is 4x; label_lease.child_cpu is the one rusage reader; label_lease.deadline budgets the suite hang guard as max(2x slowest wall, 4x slowest CPU) from the ledger user+sys columns and skips pre-probe rows rather than reading them as zero; suite_run prints wall and CPU on a timeout. AND THE FILING ITSELF HIT THE CLASS ONE LAYER DOWN: witness_resolves probed under a bare 60s wall timeout and printed a TimeoutExpired as exits-2 no-witness while this witness passes in 86s; the probe now carries its cause (hang guard crossed, CPU burned) and the guard is HANG_MULTIPLE x a CPU ceiling. 41/41, 26/26, 15/15, 16/16, 29/29. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): W8 ruled 2026-09-20: use CPU time for the timing gate, not wall. sync_verdict judged the apex gate over a 120s WALL ceiling and recorded three crossings (120.2s quiet, 120.3s alone, 46s a minute earlier) for unchanged work; measured alone after the repair it reads 54.7s wall / 54.6s CPU, CPU-bound and under the ceiling. Repair: the ceiling is CPU (rusage of the child, user+sys, one reader in label_lease.child_cpu), the wall is a hang guard at 4x the ceiling, every row carries both clocks, a wall kill reports the CPU it burned so a hang (no CPU) and a runaway (all CPU) stop sharing a line. label_lease.deadline budgets the suite hang guard as max(2x slowest wall, 4x slowest CPU) from the ledger user+sys columns, skipping pre-probe rows rather than reading them as zero; suite_run prints wall and CPU on a timeout. 41/41, 26/26, 15/15.}
}
